==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|en|reptile|-ian}}, replacing earlier {{m|en|reptilious}} and adjectival {{m|en|reptile}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ɹepˈtɪliən/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-reptilian.wav|Audio (UK)}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ɹɛpˈtɪljən/|/ɹɛpˈtɪliən/}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{lb|en|zoology}} Of or [[relating]] to the [[member]]s of the [[class]] ''[[Reptilia]]''.
# [[reptilelike|Reptilelike]].
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} [[unthinking|Unthinking]], [[low]], [[base]], [[contemptible]].
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} [[cold-blooded|Cold-blooded]], [[treacherous]], [[unavoidably]] [[selfish]] and [[hostile]].

